WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.630
London, 1599.

2
00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:07.080
A playhouse fills, and on
its stage, a ruler falls.

3
00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:12.870
Before the deed, one killer had asked:
"Shall Rome stand under one man’s awe?"

4
00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:16.470
Outside, England's own
queen is in her mid-sixties,

5
00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:19.810
unmarried and childless,
with no named heir.

6
00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:24.260
So why stage a ruler's murder
in that year of all years?

7
00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:30.010
In this mission, you'll uncover a 1571
law that made succession talk risky.

8
00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:33.120
You'll follow Rome
afterwards: a crowd turned,

9
00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:36.570
a poet attacked by a mob, armies marching.

10
00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:40.230
And you'll weigh two ways the
first audience might have taken it.

11
00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:44.960
Your mission: work out why a play
like this was staged in 1599.
